Xanthobacter_chromosome	Prodigal_v2.6.3	CDS	3059168	3060307	229.5	+	0	ID=1_2796	partial=00	start_type=ATG	rbs_motif=AGxAGG/AGGxGG	rbs_spacer=5-10bp	gc_cont=0.688	conf=99.99	score=229.49	cscore=221.59	sscore=7.90	rscore=2.74	uscore=0.10	tscore=3.77	em_ID=Xanthobacter_chromosome_2796	em_target=78245.Xaut_4271	em_score=680.0	em_evalue=1.34e-246	em_tcov=97.9	em_OGs=COG0343@1|root,COG0343@2|Bacteria,1MUCA@1224|Proteobacteria,2TR87@28211|Alphaproteobacteria,3EYJ7@335928|Xanthobacteraceae	em_COG_cat=J	em_desc=Catalyzes the base-exchange of a guanine (G) residue with the queuine precursor 7-aminomethyl-7-deazaguanine (PreQ1) at position 34 (anticodon wobble position) in tRNAs with GU(N) anticodons (tRNA-Asp, -Asn, -His and -Tyr). Catalysis occurs through a double-displacement mechanism. The nucleophile active site attacks the C1' of nucleotide 34 to detach the guanine base from the RNA, forming a covalent enzyme-RNA intermediate. The proton acceptor active site deprotonates the incoming PreQ1, allowing a nucleophilic attack on the C1' of the ribose to form the product. After dissociation, two additional enzymatic reactions on the tRNA convert PreQ1 to queuine (Q), resulting in the hypermodified nucleoside queuosine (7-(((4,5-cis-dihydroxy-2- cyclopenten-1-yl)amino)methyl)-7-deazaguanosine)	em_max_annot_lvl=28211|Alphaproteobacteria	em_Preferred_name=tgt	em_PFAMs=TGT	em_EC=2.4.2.29	em_KEGG_ko=ko:K00773	em_KEGG_Reaction=R03789,R10209	em_KEGG_rclass=RC00063	em_BRITE=ko00000,ko01000,ko03016	em_GOs=				
